igLoader TOML parsing** (from Approach 1) \n- **Data type conversion layer** (new requirement)\n- **Minimal API changes** with defensive type handling\n\n**Estimated Impact:**\n- **Files changed**: 3-4 (session.py, configloader.py, exceptions.py, requirements)\n- **Call sites affected**: 10-15 (only those handling boolean/numeric config values)\n- **New functions**: 5-7 (TOML parsing, type conversion, file discovery)\n\n## **Key Insight**\n\n**The original constraint of \"no API changes\" was based on incorrect assumptions.** The SEP's requirement for native TOML data types makes some level of API evolution unavoidable. The goal should be **minimal, backward-compatible changes** rather than zero changes.\n\n**Bottom Line**: A successful implementation requires accepting that TOML support necessitates architectural modifications, but these can be minimized through careful design and defensive programming practices.\n[Tool uses: none]",
